  "report_period": "Week 44 (23rd Oct to 30th Oct 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "F-Maritime have committed their Kamsarmax \"Panorama\" 81/2012 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 02/2027) to undisclosed interests at USD 20,5 mill. By way of comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Daebo Gladstone\" 81/2013 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 12/2028) was sold in September at USD 22,5 mill. The Panamax \"Amoy Sunny\" 76/2006 Imabari, Japan (SS 06/2031, DD 09/2029) of Amoysailing Maritime was committed at USD 13,8 mill. Note that the one-year-older sister vessel \"Sea Orion\" 76/2005 Imabari, Japan (SS 01/2030, DD 12/2027) was sold in September at USD 11,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, Japanese owners committed the \"Charade\" 58/2013 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 08/2030, DD 07/2028) at USD 22,8 mill. For reference, the two-years-older \"Kristinita\" 58/2011 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 07/2031, DD 05/2029) was committed at week ago at xs USD 20 mill. Furthermore, the \"Saltwind Explorer\" 55/2011 Hyundai- Vinashin, Vietnam (SS 01/2031, DD 01/2029) was committed to clients of Transworld at USD 16,5 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the one-year- younger sister vessel \"Prometheus 1\" 55/2012 Hyundai-Vinashin, Vietnam (SS/DD 09/2027) was sold at USD 19 mill. In addition, Spar Shipping committed their \"Spar Gemini\" 53/2007 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 02/2027) to Chinese interests at USD 12,4 mill, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"Spar Scorpio\" 53/2006 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 10/2026) was sold a couple of months ago at USD 11,35 mill. Union Commercial have committed their Handysize \"Union Taylor\" 37/2014 Shimanami, Japan (SS 09/2029, DD 10/2027) at USD 22 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Locomotion\" 38/2013 Shimanami, Japan (SS 12/2030, DD 12/2028) was sold at USD 19,8 mill. Moreover, Astrobulk committed the OHBS \"Astro Polaris\" 37/2014 Onomichi, Japan (SS 09/2029, DD 10/2027) to Greek interests at high USD 19 mill. Remind you that back in September, the one-year-older \"Ansac Pride\" 37/2013 Onomichi, Japan (SS/DD 06/2028, OHBS) was sold at USD 18,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "The Suezmax \"Advantage Spice\" 156/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 02/2030, DD 12/2027, Scrubber fitted) was committed at USD 97,5 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the sister vessel \"Advantage Summer\" 156/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 06/2030, DD 10/2028, Scrubber fitted) was committed at the same price.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia to China route strengthened, with Dampier and Port Hedland fixtures settling between USD 13.80/15.10 fio. In the Atlantic, long-haul business from Tubarao to Qingdao, including West Africa options, pushed higher to USD 36.00/36.60 fio. Transatlantic and long- haul departures from Seven Islands to Far East destinations achieved strong levels between USD 39.25/39.75 fio, while a Nouadhibou run to Qingdao made USD 34.15 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, NoPac trips with Singapore-Japan and Persian Gulf options settled between USD 17,500/19,250 pd. Australian rounds with redelivery in China and Singapore-Japan ranges fetched between USD 17,000/24,500 pd. Indonesian coal runs to South China achieved between USD 13,000/17,000 pd, alongside a coastal ECI trip fixing at USD 16,900 pd. From East Coast India, Japan and South East Asia, trips via ECSA to Singapore-Japan range fixed between USD 17,000/21,000 pd, while a direct ECSA front-haul reached USD 18,000 pd alongside an $800,000 ballast bonus. Out of West Coast India, runs via South Africa to India range obtained between USD 18,500/19,500 pd. In the Atlantic, a West Med bauxite trip via West Africa to Continent made USD 22,500 pd, while a Continent departure via USEC to Singapore-Japan reached USD 28,350 pd.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, Indonesian coal trips to SE Asia, China and India ranges settled between USD 20,000/25,000 pd, while limestone runs to ECI achieved between USD 27,000/32,000 pd. Australian rounds with redelivery in China, Japan, ECI and SE Asia ranges fetched between USD 21,000/26,500 pd. NoPac and clinker runs to SE Asia obtained USD 21,000 pd and USD 22,750 pd respectively. Long-haul trips from China to West Africa reached USD 28,000 pd, while a Japan departure via China to Mediterranean made USD 25,500 pd. In the Atlantic, US Gulf front-haul petcoke and grain trips to Far East and India fixed between USD 28,500/32,000 pd, alongside transatlantic wood pellets to Continent at USD 31,000 pd. Out of WCSA and ECSA, front- haul departures to Far East range achieved between USD 19,750/30,250 pd. On period, several Ultramaxes fixed for 3 to 7 months duration between USD 23,000/24,500 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Limited reported activity was recorded in the sector this week. In the Atlantic, a US Gulf departure to NCSA range fixed at USD 16,000 pd. On period, a Handysize delivering in ECSA was secured for 5 to 7 months duration in the Atlantic at USD 20,800 pd."
    }
  },
